{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1198335-changeling-the-dreaming-fiction","id":1198335,"title":"Changeling: The Dreaming Fiction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-22T08:56:10-07:00","id":1198335,"title":"Changeling: The Dreaming Fiction","content":"I'm trying to compile a list of all the <i>Changeling: The Dreaming</i> fiction that was published by White Wolf in the 1990s. So far I have found the following:<ul><li>Jackie Cassada's <i>The Immortal Eyes Trilogy </i>(<a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/1258552.The_Toybox?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\">The Toybox</a>, <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/421826.Shadows_on_the_Hill\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Shadows on the Hill</i></a>, and <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/999088.Court_of_All_Kings\" target=\"_blank\">Court of All Kings</a>)</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/336949.The_Splendour_Falls?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Splendour Falls</i></a>, a Changeling anthology edited by Erin Kelly</li> <li>Don Bassingthwaite's <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/1258564.Pomegranates_Full_and_Fine?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Pomegranates Full and Fine</i></a></li> <li>Esther Friesner's <i>Playing with Fire</i>, in <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/336950.The_Essential_World_of_Darkness_World_of_Darkness?ac=1&amp;from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Essential World of Darkness</i></a>, edited by Stewart Wieck and Anna Branscome</li> <li>Jody Lynn Nye's <i>The Muse</i>, in <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/1253336.The_Quintessential_World_of_Darkness?ac=1&amp;from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Quintessential World of Darkness</i></a>, edited by Stewart Wieck and Anna Branscome</li> <li>Some stories in the anthology <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/1831746.Strange_City\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Strange City</i></a><i>, </i>edited by Staley Krause and Stewart Wieck.</li> </ul><br /> According to Goodreads, the anthology <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/336946.City_of_Darkness\" target=\"_blank\"><i>City of Darkness: Unseen</i></a> is also a Changeling book, but as far as I can tell, this seems to be only about Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Wraith, <i>not </i>Changeling. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> (Also, Onyx Path recently published the <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/35481865-anthology-of-dreams?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Anthology of Dreams</i></a>, edited by Matthew McFarland.)<br /> <br /> Am I missing any others, either short stories or novels? Are there any Changeling stories in World of Darkness anthologies that are primarily set in the other lines?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","name":"darkyeoman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}